# 4. REVIEW COMPLETION TRUTH TABLE

Produce a source-backed truth table covering at least:

| Scenario | Review completion | Criterion result |
|---|---|---|
| No human judgments | Not reviewed | Undetermined |
| Some required judgments unresolved | In progress | Undetermined unless conclusively resolved by approved rules |
| All relevant requirements evaluated and passed | Complete | Pass |
| All relevant requirements resolved, one mandatory requirement failed | Complete | Fail |
| Optional alternative not selected | Does not create outstanding review work | Not automatically Fail |
| Sufficient alternatives passed | Complete if no other required work remains | Pass |
| Some alternatives failed, others unresolved | Depends on whether the requirement can be conclusively resolved | Undetermined or Fail only when justified |
| All valid alternatives assessed as failing | Complete | Fail |
| Active supplementation request | Supplementation pending | Preserve last judgment and pending state according to the canonical contract |
| Supplement returned but not reassessed | Pending reassessment | Do not silently treat as newly passed |
| Previously passed judgment edited to Fail | Recalculate | Recalculate safely |

Do not blindly hardcode this table without checking actual domain rules.

Specify the evidence required to consider a criterion conclusively failed.

Where a requirement is already satisfied by one qualifying alternative, unselected optional alternatives must not be counted as outstanding work.

Where extra submitted declarations remain unresolved, verify whether they are mandatory to review before declaring the entire criterion complete.

Do not invent a requirement to reject irrelevant alternatives.

