# 7. CRITICAL CORRECTION — NO AUTOMATIC OFFICIAL WORKFLOW DECISIONS

LEAN-0 proposes automatic status changes when all five criteria meet the requirements.

This must be carefully separated into two categories.

## Allowed derived updates

The system may automatically derive:

- Human-reviewed criteria count.
- Criteria meeting requirements count.
- Criteria failing requirements count.
- Criterion evaluation result.
- Review progress.
- Whether all required assessment work is resolved.
- Preliminary eligibility indication.

Only where canonical business rules make those values determinable.

## Not automatically authorized

The system must NOT automatically:

- Submit an application on behalf of a Student.
- Record a School recommendation.
- Select every eligible application for forwarding.
- Forward a School batch to City.
- Record the City reviewer's official completion/attestation if it represents a separate authorized action.
- Make a Committee decision.
- Issue an official decision document.
- Publish recognition results.

Do not turn "5/5 criteria passed" into an official human recommendation or recognition.

### School

A dossier with five passing criteria can be marked:

"Đủ điều kiện theo kết quả sơ tuyển"

where supported.

But School recommendation and batch selection must remain appropriate authorized actions.

A School may need to record "Đề nghị" or "Không đề nghị" separately.

Do not remove that authority without an approved contract.

### City

The City independently reviews received applications.

Automatically deriving five criterion outcomes is acceptable.

But inspect whether the final City review completion is a required separate human attestation.

If it is, preserve it.

Do not automatically send an application to Committee merely because five criteria pass.

### Committee

Only authorized Committee actions may record official recognition.

No automatic official approval.

